{"title":"2023 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 4","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_CoolMathProblems\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by CoolMathProblems</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(A_Clever_Explanation_You’ll_Get_Instantly)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (A Clever Explanation You’ll Get Instantly)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Simple,_Intuitive_Solution_by_MathTalks_Now\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Simple, Intuitive Solution by MathTalks_Now</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(How_to_Creatively_THINK!!!)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (How to Creatively THINK!!!)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Math-X_(Smart_and_Simple)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Math-X (Smart and Simple)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Magic_Square\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Magic Square</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_SpreadTheMathLove\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by SpreadTheMathLove</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Interstigation\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">12</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Interstigation</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-13\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_WhyMath\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">13</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by WhyMath</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-14\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_harungurcan\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">14</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by harungurcan</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-15\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Dr._David\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">15</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Dr. David</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-16\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution!_Super_Easy_to_Understand_and_Cleverly_Fast_and_Smart!\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">16</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution! Super Easy to Understand and Cleverly Fast and Smart!</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-17\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_SquishBJ_(AIME_Qualifier)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">17</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by SquishBJ (AIME Qualifier)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-18\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_in_Chinese_by_SquishBJ_(AIME_Qualifier)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">18</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution in Chinese by SquishBJ (AIME Qualifier)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-19\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">19</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The numbers from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/c/34c8e6bf4d57cd6f2bb0d7d43e00f0f442f53b84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$49$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"17\" height=\"13\" /> are arranged in a spiral pattern on a square grid, beginning at the center. The first few numbers have been entered into the grid below. Consider the four numbers that will appear in the shaded squares, on the same diagonal as the number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/7/b17ce6fcb2994d4241d780dd5311d828db133411.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7.$\" width=\"12\" height=\"12\" /> How many of these four numbers are prime?\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/8/6e88180afd53a16ea3b9e0389e44933a31876e70.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] /* Made by MRENTHUSIASM */ size(175);  void ds(pair p) { \tfilldraw((0.5,0.5)+p--(-0.5,0.5)+p--(-0.5,-0.5)+p--(0.5,-0.5)+p--cycle,mediumgrey); }  ds((0.5,4.5)); ds((1.5,3.5)); ds((3.5,1.5)); ds((4.5,0.5));  add(grid(7,7,grey+linewidth(1.25)));  int adj = 1; int curUp = 2; int curLeft = 4; int curDown = 6;  label(&quot;$1$&quot;,(3.5,3.5));  for (int len = 3; len&lt;=3; len+=2) { \tfor (int i=1; i&lt;=len-1; ++i)     \t\t{ \t\t\tlabel(&quot;$&quot;+string(curUp)+&quot;$&quot;,(3.5+adj,3.5-adj+i));     \t\tlabel(&quot;$&quot;+string(curLeft)+&quot;$&quot;,(3.5+adj-i,3.5+adj));      \t\tlabel(&quot;$&quot;+string(curDown)+&quot;$&quot;,(3.5-adj,3.5+adj-i));     \t\t++curDown;     \t\t++curLeft;     \t\t++curUp; \t\t} \t++adj;     curUp = len^2 + 1;     curLeft = len^2 + len + 2;     curDown = len^2 + 2*len + 3; }  draw((4,4)--(3,4)--(3,3)--(5,3)--(5,5)--(2,5)--(2,2)--(6,2)--(6,6)--(1,6)--(1,1)--(7,1)--(7,7)--(0,7)--(0,0)--(7,0),linewidth(2)); [/asy]\" width=\"292\" height=\"292\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/c/0bcd5bbd626bd1e1ecd06b5e602defd55c570b1f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 0 \\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ 1 \\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\ 2 \\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\ 3 \\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\ 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"351\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We fill out the grid, as shown below:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/c/6ec6820e4734959c2e1ea32455e6e37e6ee38967.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] /* Made by MRENTHUSIASM */ size(175);  void ds(pair p) { \tfilldraw((0.5,0.5)+p--(-0.5,0.5)+p--(-0.5,-0.5)+p--(0.5,-0.5)+p--cycle,mediumgrey); }  ds((0.5,4.5)); ds((1.5,3.5)); ds((3.5,1.5)); ds((4.5,0.5));  add(grid(7,7,grey+linewidth(1.25)));  int adj = 1; int curUp = 2; int curLeft = 4; int curDown = 6; int curRight = 8;  label(&quot;$1$&quot;,(3.5,3.5));  for (int len = 3; len&lt;=7; len+=2) { \tfor (int i=1; i&lt;=len-1; ++i)     \t\t{ \t\t\tlabel(&quot;$&quot;+string(curUp)+&quot;$&quot;,(3.5+adj,3.5-adj+i));     \t\tlabel(&quot;$&quot;+string(curLeft)+&quot;$&quot;,(3.5+adj-i,3.5+adj));      \t\tlabel(&quot;$&quot;+string(curDown)+&quot;$&quot;,(3.5-adj,3.5+adj-i));     \t\tlabel(&quot;$&quot;+string(curRight)+&quot;$&quot;,(3.5-adj+i,3.5-adj));     \t\t++curDown;     \t\t++curLeft;     \t\t++curUp;     \t\t++curRight; \t\t} \t++adj;     curUp = len^2 + 1;     curLeft = len^2 + len + 2;     curDown = len^2 + 2*len + 3;     curRight = len^2 + 3*len + 4; }  draw((4,4)--(3,4)--(3,3)--(5,3)--(5,5)--(2,5)--(2,2)--(6,2)--(6,6)--(1,6)--(1,1)--(7,1)--(7,7)--(0,7)--(0,0)--(7,0),linewidth(2)); [/asy]\" width=\"292\" height=\"292\" />\nFrom the four numbers that appear in the shaded squares, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/a/02af645f20a9874a363187aa704686ebf6104a6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}\\ 3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"55\" height=\"28\" /> of them are prime: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/3/45378034a4897f58209cf8faa61ce2a2a342548a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$19,23,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"51\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/d/c8d06fc910703a003655e44dbcd4f3626ee6d02f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$47.$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"21\" height=\"12\" />\n</p><p>~MathFun1000, MRENTHUSIASM\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Note that given time constraint, it's better to only count from perfect squares (in pink), as shown below:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/5/22579266b483266ee0dff48378bb0dd384c538a4.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] /* Grid Made by MRENTHUSIASM */ /* Squares pattern solution input by TheMathGuyd */ size(175);  void ds(pair p) { \tfilldraw((0.5,0.5)+p--(-0.5,0.5)+p--(-0.5,-0.5)+p--(0.5,-0.5)+p--cycle,mediumgrey); }  void ps(pair p) { \tfilldraw((0.5,0.5)+p--(-0.5,0.5)+p--(-0.5,-0.5)+p--(0.5,-0.5)+p--cycle,pink+opacity(0.3)); } real ts = 0.5;  ds((0.5,4.5));label(&quot;$39$&quot;,(0.5,4.5)); ds((1.5,3.5));label(&quot;$19$&quot;,(1.5,3.5)); ds((3.5,1.5));label(&quot;$23$&quot;,(3.5,1.5)); ds((4.5,0.5));label(&quot;$47$&quot;,(4.5,0.5));  ps((3.5,3.5));label(&quot;$1$&quot;,(3.5,3.5)); ps((4.5,2.5));label(&quot;$9$&quot;,(4.5,2.5)); ps((5.5,1.5));label(&quot;$25$&quot;,(5.5,1.5)); ps((6.5,0.5));label(&quot;$49$&quot;,(6.5,0.5)); ps((3.5,4.5));label(&quot;$4$&quot;,(3.5,4.5)); ps((2.5,5.5));label(&quot;$16$&quot;,(2.5,5.5)); ps((1.5,6.5));label(&quot;$36$&quot;,(1.5,6.5)); label(scale(ts)*&quot;$\\leftarrow$&quot;,(1,6),NE); label(scale(ts)*&quot;$+1$&quot;,(1,6),NW); label(scale(ts)*&quot;$\\downarrow$&quot;,(1,6),SW); label(scale(ts)*&quot;$+2$&quot;,(1,5),NW); label(scale(ts)*&quot;$\\downarrow$&quot;,(1,5),SW); label(scale(ts)*&quot;$+3$&quot;,(1,4),NW); label(scale(ts)*&quot;$+1$&quot;,(2,5),NW); label(scale(ts)*&quot;$\\downarrow$&quot;,(2,5),SW); label(scale(ts)*&quot;$+2$&quot;,(2,4),NW); label(scale(ts)*&quot;$\\downarrow$&quot;,(2,4),SW); label(scale(ts)*&quot;$+3$&quot;,(2,3),NW);  label(scale(ts)*&quot;$\\leftarrow$&quot;,(5,1),NE); label(scale(ts)*&quot;$-1$&quot;,(5,1),NW); label(scale(ts)*&quot;$\\leftarrow$&quot;,(4,1),NE); label(scale(ts)*&quot;$-2$&quot;,(4,1),NW); label(scale(ts)*&quot;$\\leftarrow$&quot;,(6,0),NE); label(scale(ts)*&quot;$-1$&quot;,(6,0),NW); label(scale(ts)*&quot;$\\leftarrow$&quot;,(5,0),NE); label(scale(ts)*&quot;$-2$&quot;,(5,0),NW);  add(grid(7,7,grey+linewidth(1.25))); //USES OLYMPIAD.ASY  draw((4,4)--(3,4)--(3,3)--(5,3)--(5,5)--(2,5)--(2,2)--(6,2)--(6,6)--(1,6)--(1,1)--(7,1)--(7,7)--(0,7)--(0,0)--(7,0),linewidth(2)); [/asy]\" width=\"292\" height=\"292\" />\nFrom the four numbers that appear in the shaded squares, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/a/02af645f20a9874a363187aa704686ebf6104a6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}\\ 3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"55\" height=\"28\" /> of them are prime: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/3/45378034a4897f58209cf8faa61ce2a2a342548a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$19,23,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"51\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/d/c8d06fc910703a003655e44dbcd4f3626ee6d02f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$47.$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"21\" height=\"12\" />\n</p><p>~TheMathGuyd\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since the last shaded square is very close to the final number, which is 49, we can easily subtract two instead of having to count all the way there. Then, we can count (:P).\n</p><p>~AliceDubbleYou\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_CoolMathProblems\">Video Solution by CoolMathProblems</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by CoolMathProblems\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/Pf93RGtKo1I?feature=shared&amp;t=190\">https://youtu.be/Pf93RGtKo1I?feature=shared&amp;t=190</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_.28A_Clever_Explanation_You.E2.80.99ll_Get_Instantly.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_(A_Clever_Explanation_You’ll_Get_Instantly)\">Video Solution (A Clever Explanation You’ll Get Instantly)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution (A Clever Explanation You’ll Get Instantly)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/zntZrtsnyxc?si=nM5eWOwNU6HRdleZ&amp;t=158\">https://youtu.be/zntZrtsnyxc?si=nM5eWOwNU6HRdleZ&amp;t=158</a>\n~hsnacademy\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Simple.2C_Intuitive_Solution_by_MathTalks_Now\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Simple,_Intuitive_Solution_by_MathTalks_Now\">Simple, Intuitive Solution by MathTalks_Now</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Simple, Intuitive Solution by MathTalks_Now\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li>*Different Solution not shown before!*</li></ul>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://studio.youtube.com/video/PMOeiGLkDH0/edit\">https://studio.youtube.com/video/PMOeiGLkDH0/edit</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_.28How_to_Creatively_THINK.21.21.21.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_(How_to_Creatively_THINK!!!)\">Video Solution (How to Creatively THINK!!!)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution (How to Creatively THINK!!!)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/7gwhzjySKl0\">https://youtu.be/7gwhzjySKl0</a>\n</p><p>~Education the Study of everything\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_by_Math-X_.28Smart_and_Simple.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Math-X_(Smart_and_Simple)\">Video